# Installed as /etc/journal-digest/ignore by install-journal-digest.sh, which overwrites edits made there.
#
# Failures and errors which journal-digest leaves out of its daily report. One Python regular expression per line,
# searched for in the line the report shows: "unit (system): result" or "unit (user): result" for a failed unit,
# "identifier: message" for an error, and "crash of executable (package): signal" for a crash report. Empty lines and
# lines starting with # are skipped.
#
# Try patterns out before installing them with: ./journal-digest.py --since -7d --ignore journal-digest.ignore

# Short-lived autostart commands which often exit before gnome-session asks systemd to move them into their scope,
# which systemd then refuses ("No PIDs left to attach"). The commands themselves ran.
^app-gnome-(ubuntu\\x2dreport\\x2don\\x2dupgrade|snap\\x2duserd\\x2dautostart)-[0-9]+\.scope \(user\): resources$
^systemd: Failed to start app-gnome-(ubuntu\\x2dreport\\x2don\\x2dupgrade|snap\\x2duserd\\x2dautostart)-[0-9]+\.scope
